Carafe: with X87FastStack, the x87 condition bits C0 to C3 written in a block are reused by later reads in the same
block instead of being loaded back from memory, and storing the same constant twice is skipped. FNSTSW after FCOM
loaded the four bits FCOM had just stored, and every FXCH stored C1 = 0 again. The bits are still stored once, so
the state seen outside the block does not change.
MIT, as the files it changes.

